<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 20.30 percent.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 20.30 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 115 basis points to 20.30 percent and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     21.45	    20.30		   -115 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     23.21	    22.20		   -101 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    24.06	    22.87		   -119 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.30	    24.00		   -130 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
